ses::Moses::reviewed_unambiguous_name","scope":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","senseReview":"Reviewed complete original name headword and source subject. Article covers the biblical person(s), named place, or named spiritual figure denoted by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Moses","term":"Moses"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Moses","sourceTitle":"Moses"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"source_verified_redirect","phrase":"Tent of Meeting","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_publisher_redirect","originalCitations":[],"ruleId":"Tabernacle::Tent of Meeting::reviewed_publisher_redirect","sourceHeadwordId":"TentofMeeting"},"text":"and they brought up the ark and the Tent of Meeting with all its sacred furnishings. The Levitical priests carried them up.","verse":5}],"id":"Tabernacle","label":"Tent of Meeting","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Tabernacle::Tent of Meeting::reviewed_publisher_redirect","scope":"reviewed_publisher_redirect","senseReview":"The original publisher explicitly links this complete unambiguous name/phrase to this target. Redirect and target were reviewed once; actual BSB phrase and full word boundaries required. Target original title and complete article remain unchanged.","sourceHeadwordId":"TentofMeeting","term":"Tent of Meeting"}],"matchingRule":"source_verified_redirect","matchingRules":["source_verified_redirect"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Tabernacle","sourceTitle":"Tabernacle"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Zion","senseEvidence":{"basis":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":5,"href":"?bref=2Chr.5.2","rawReference":"2Chr.5.2"}],"ruleId":"Zion::Zion::reviewed_unambiguous_name","sourceHeadwordId":"Zion"},"text":"At that time Solomon assembled in Jerusalem the elders of Israel—all the tribal heads and family leaders of the Israelites—to bring up the ark of the covenant of the LORD from Zion, the City of David.","verse":2}],"id":"Zion","label":"Zion","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Zion::Zion::reviewed_unambiguous_name","scope":"reviewed_unambiguous_name","senseReview":"Reviewed complete original name headword and source subject. Article covers the biblical person(s), named place, or named spiritual figure denoted by this exact spelling; multiple persons under one unchanged source article remain together. Actual proper-name capitalization and whole-name boundaries required. Explicit occurrence-level ambiguity exclusions override this rule.","sourceHeadwordId":"Zion","term":"Zion"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Zion","sourceTitle":"Zion"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.5.1","r":"2Chr.5.1","rawR":"2Chr.5.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.5.1","value":"2Chr.5.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:1"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," This verse concludes the section on Temple furnishings, following ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.7.51","r":"1Kgs.7.51","rawR":"1Kgs.7.51","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.7.51","value":"1Kgs.7.51"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 7:51"}," almost verbatim. • ",{"c":["the gifts his father, David, had dedicated:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," Just as the spoils taken from Egypt went into building the Tabernacle, the spoils of Israel’s enemies built ",{"c":["the Temple"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},". The prophets often portrayed the spoils of other nations as being at Israel’s disposal (see ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.60.10-14","r":"Isa.60.10-14","rawR":"Isa.60.10-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.60.10-14","value":"Isa.60.10-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isa 60:10-14"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Zech.14.14","r":"Zech.14.14","rawR":"Zech.14.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Zech.14.14","value":"Zech.14.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"Zech 14:14"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.5.1","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":5,"endVerse":1,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.5.1","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"cdf5cb64838013024fbc1b400d723e3a86d4d8ed1025c7f7a63e52d5de7c85d1","sourceItemName":"IIChr.5.1","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4921,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.5.1","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.5.1","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.5.3","r":"2Chr.5.3","rawR":"2Chr.5.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.5.3","value":"2Chr.5.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The dedication of the Temple took place during ",{"c":["the annual Festival of Shelters, which is held in early autumn."],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," This seven-day festival required a pilgrimage to the central place of worship (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.16.13-15","r":"Deut.16.13-15","rawR":"Deut.16.13-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.16.13-15","value":"Deut.16.13-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Deut 16:13-15"},"). The seventh month marked the end of Israel’s harvest season, allowing landowners to leave for a week without concern for fields or crops."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.5.3","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":5,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.5.3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7d965c4cd1aed5a2acb54615c88a91aef9f1f58058d17ad212aafd0f5babebc2","sourceItemName":"IIChr.5.3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4922,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.5.3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.5.3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.5.5","r":"2Chr.5.5","rawR":"2Chr.5.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.5.5","value":"2Chr.5.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:5"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["the special tent:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," “Tent of Meeting” is the name used in Exodus to indicate the function of the Tabernacle (e.g., ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.33.7","r":"Exod.33.7","rawR":"Exod.33.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.33.7","value":"Exod.33.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 33:7"},"). The Tabernacle was the dwelling place of the divine presence (e.g., ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.25.8-9","r":"Exod.25.8-9","rawR":"Exod.25.8-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.25.8-9","value":"Exod.25.8-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 25:8-9"},") and the place where God met with his people through the priests. After the Temple was built, this special tent had no further function."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.5.5","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":5,"endVerse":5,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":5}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.5.5","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"fd96e2c7d265b9a67ff67183280aa32d7ac03ddc13fdcc0380432834e7aaa731","sourceItemName":"IIChr.5.5","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4923,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.5.5","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.5.5","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.5.7-8","r":"2Chr.5.7-8","rawR":"2Chr.5.7-8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.5.7-8","value":"2Chr.5.7-8"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:7-8"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The giant ",{"c":["cherubim"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," were symbols of the universal and eternal rule of God."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.5.7-8","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":5,"endVerse":8,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":7}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.5.7-8","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"edef5a25c650ec6b378c101c41a653c7d269cafc920f3488b472ede17038a792","sourceItemName":"IIChr.5.7-8","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4924,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.5.7-8","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.5.7-8","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.5.9","r":"2Chr.5.9","rawR":"2Chr.5.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.5.9","value":"2Chr.5.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:9"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The Hebrew phrase ",{"c":["to this day"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," might be an idiom meaning ",{"c":["from then on."],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," The Ark was evidently not in the Temple following the Exile, when the Chronicler wrote."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.5.9","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":5,"endVerse":9,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":9}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.5.9","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3273574a67db50ba70f722a1c9a67a1c7028cb9ea1562f0b36daf5fe2192a25b","sourceItemName":"IIChr.5.9","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4925,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.5.9","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.5.9","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.5.10","r":"2Chr.5.10","rawR":"2Chr.5.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.5.10","value":"2Chr.5.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:10"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The ",{"c":["Ark"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," contained only the ",{"c":["tablets"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," of the covenant (see ",{"href":"?bref=Exod.25.21","r":"Exod.25.21","rawR":"Exod.25.21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.25.21","value":"Exod.25.21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 25:21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.10.5","r":"Deut.10.5","rawR":"Deut.10.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.10.5","value":"Deut.10.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Deut 10:5"},"). The pot of manna Aaron placed in the Ark (",{"href":"?bref=Exod.16.33-34","r":"Exod.16.33-34","rawR":"Exod.16.33-34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Exod.16.33-34","value":"Exod.16.33-34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Exod 16:33-34"},") had apparently been lost."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.5.10","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":5,"endVerse":10,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":10}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.5.10","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"7037cd2896840b349ae48d41f570e81f69c055661eee4ee24fd2c8f1be19c211","sourceItemName":"IIChr.5.10","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4926,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.5.10","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.5.10","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.5.11-14","r":"2Chr.5.11-14","rawR":"2Chr.5.11-14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.5.11-14","value":"2Chr.5.11-14"}],"t":"ref","v":"5:11-14"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The Chronicler complements the dedication of the Temple with a detailed description of a great celebration. He names the three specific orders of ",{"c":["singers"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," and all their kinsmen. The ",{"c":["120 . . . trumpeters"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," apparently included five priests from each of the 24 divisions (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.24.3-19","r":"1Chr.24.3-19","rawR":"1Chr.24.3-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.24.3-19","value":"1Chr.24.3-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 24:3-19"},"). The sanctified priests, their standard apparel of ",{"c":["fine linen robes"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," the musical ",{"c":["instruments"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," the singers, and the trumpeters were all correctly positioned. When the priests exited, the musicians raised their song, and the ",{"c":["cloud"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," of the ",{"c":["glorious presence of the"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Lord"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt-divine-name","t":"span"},{"c":[" filled the Temple."],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.5.11-14","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":5,"endVerse":14,"startChapter":5,"startVerse":11}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.5.11-14","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[5],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"505783f56e92a2c8414b3c259983e8e120e98b74300693d6d18566eb8ea09407","sourceItemName":"IIChr.5.11-14","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4927,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.5.11-14","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.5.11-14","type":"StudyNote"}],"version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}